      "Language": "nor",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The article focuses on the pathophysiology of pain as a result of injury to the peripheral or central nervous system. The nervous system is dynamic, and nerve injury leads to long-lasting changes in the nociceptive neurons. Plasticity in the neuronal systems regulating nociception is important in explaining clinical features associated with nerve injury pain. To treat nerve injury pain more effectively, measures should be taken to both prevent and reverse the functional neuronal changes and plasticity caused by nerve injury."},
